WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:05.680
By now, there have been so many remakes, reboots,
and unnecessary sequels to our favorite 80s

00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:09.650
action movies that it's inevitable some of
them are going to be pretty subpar.

00:00:09.650 --> 00:00:14.130
But there's plenty of reason to believe The
Predator will do right by its predecessors.

00:00:14.130 --> 00:00:18.310
Stacked with top-shelf talent both in front
of and behind the camera, The Predator is

00:00:18.310 --> 00:00:22.679
neither a direct continuation of the original
films nor a total reboot.

00:00:22.679 --> 00:00:26.980
Set in the same universe, it's trying a story
that's completely new, and unlike the Alien

00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:30.150
vs. Predator movies, it actually looks kind
of good.

00:00:30.150 --> 00:00:33.250
Here's why we think The Predator will blow
us away.

00:00:33.250 --> 00:00:35.410
Resistance is futile

00:00:35.410 --> 00:00:39.820
The alien hunters of the original Predator
movies are, to put it mildly, pretty formidable

00:00:39.820 --> 00:00:40.820
warriors.

00:00:40.820 --> 00:00:45.320
They're strong, fast, can camouflage themselves,
and have weapons capable of blasting a hole

00:00:45.320 --> 00:00:48.390
the size of a watermelon in Jesse Ventura's
torso.

00:00:48.390 --> 00:00:52.470
If that was all the heroes of the new film
had to face, things would be tough enough.

00:00:52.470 --> 00:00:56.560
But the extraterrestrial hunters of the new
film appear to be next-level specimens, and

00:00:56.560 --> 00:00:58.760
they don't just hunt for the thrill of it.

00:00:58.760 --> 00:01:03.610
This time around, the Predators have genetically
upgraded themselves with DNA from other species,

00:01:03.610 --> 00:01:04.809
assimilating their prey.

00:01:04.809 --> 00:01:09.240
It's a development which seems to imply that,
like the cybernetic Borg of Star Trek fame,

00:01:09.240 --> 00:01:12.030
the Predators now absorb the strengths of
their conquered.

00:01:12.030 --> 00:01:16.200
If the Predators end up with more diverse
upgrades than just "the same, but bigger,"

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:19.990
fans might get to enjoy puzzling out which
species they get their new powers from.

00:01:19.990 --> 00:01:24.020
We know the hunters have encountered the xenomorphs
of the Alien franchise, after all.

00:01:24.020 --> 00:01:28.939
Imagine if a Predator had acid blood, or,
even scarier, a baby mouth inside its regular

00:01:28.939 --> 00:01:29.939
mouth?

00:01:29.939 --> 00:01:34.079
After three movies and two crossovers, we'd
finally see true horror.

00:01:34.079 --> 00:01:35.840
Evolution of the hunt

00:01:35.840 --> 00:01:39.770
The new Predator is being directed by Shane
Black, the famed screenwriter behind Lethal

00:01:39.770 --> 00:01:42.520
Weapon who came to fame in the late 80s.

00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:45.770
His sharp dialogue is a highlight of even
his weakest screenplays.

00:01:45.770 --> 00:01:50.790
He's also proven himself to be a capable director,
getting behind the camera for Iron Man 3,

00:01:50.790 --> 00:01:53.049
Kiss Kiss Bang Bang, and The Nice Guys.

00:01:53.049 --> 00:01:57.450
He even has a little insight into the franchise
he inherited, being with it from the start.

00:01:57.450 --> 00:02:02.119
He actually appeared as an actor in the original
Predator, a bit part, since the Predator chose

00:02:02.119 --> 00:02:03.829
his character as a first target.

00:02:03.829 --> 00:02:08.369
During a talk with Collider, Black gave some
indication of exactly how his new Predator

00:02:08.369 --> 00:02:12.620
would pay respect to what came before while
improving on it at the same time.

00:02:12.620 --> 00:02:13.620
Black said,

00:02:13.620 --> 00:02:16.920
"We just tried to take the existing mythology
and take it a step further.

00:02:16.920 --> 00:02:18.510
Ask some questions about why?

00:02:18.510 --> 00:02:20.330
Why do Predators do what they do?

00:02:20.330 --> 00:02:21.810
What would be the next step for them?

00:02:21.810 --> 00:02:25.129
How do we up the stakes so that there’s
not just a single Predator hunting a group

00:02:25.129 --> 00:02:26.230
of soldiers?"

00:02:26.230 --> 00:02:29.830
Black's comments paint a picture of a new
class of predator that's more ambitious than

00:02:29.830 --> 00:02:34.360
audiences are used to, implying that the aliens
aren't just out for sport this time.

00:02:34.360 --> 00:02:37.370
Their goals now may be closer to world domination.

00:02:37.370 --> 00:02:39.200
A different kind of cast

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:43.250
The original Predator focused on a group of
elite soldiers on a rescue mission.

00:02:43.250 --> 00:02:47.569
Despite how capable each soldier was, most
of the times the Predator killed off one of

00:02:47.569 --> 00:02:49.549
them when they were separated from the team.

00:02:49.549 --> 00:02:52.860
If Dutch and the gang weren't trying to outdo
each other's machismo and

00:02:52.860 --> 00:02:56.960
had better group chemistry and camaraderie,
the Predator wouldn't have had such a staggering

00:02:56.960 --> 00:02:59.239
body count by the end of the movie.

00:02:59.239 --> 00:03:01.969
That likely won't be a problem with The Predator.

00:03:01.969 --> 00:03:06.380
Cast member Sterling K. Brown has praised
the movie for fostering a sense of, quote,

00:03:06.380 --> 00:03:07.739
"real camaraderie."

00:03:07.739 --> 00:03:12.030
No doubt this is partially due to the script
and Black's direction, but the movie's also

00:03:12.030 --> 00:03:16.409
got a unique cast with some unexpected players
that we can't wait to see bounce off of each

00:03:16.409 --> 00:03:17.409
other.

00:03:17.409 --> 00:03:20.579
Some of the more out-there actors to see in
a Predator movie include Alfie Allen from

00:03:20.579 --> 00:03:26.610
Game of Thrones, comedian Keegan-Michael Key,
and Trevante Rhodes from Moonlight, the 2017

00:03:26.610 --> 00:03:27.930
Best Picture winner.

00:03:27.930 --> 00:03:32.890
Even young Jacob Tremblay from Room will apparently
play a big part in fending off the Predators,

00:03:32.890 --> 00:03:35.239
due to an ability to quickly learn languages.

00:03:35.239 --> 00:03:39.670
While the first Predator movie was all testosterone,
this is a cast that can approach the material

00:03:39.670 --> 00:03:44.489
from different directions, from the dramatic,
to the childlike, to the wickedly funny.

00:03:44.489 --> 00:03:46.180
"Would you let me date your daughter?"

00:03:46.180 --> 00:03:46.880
"Of course!"

00:03:53.660 --> 00:03:55.300
Witty weirdness

00:03:55.310 --> 00:03:59.829
While the first Predator movie can be an amusing
watch today, it's not necessarily funny on

00:03:59.829 --> 00:04:04.490
purpose, finding laughs in over-the-top machismo
rather than actual jokes.

00:04:04.490 --> 00:04:08.129
That looks like it'll be different in this
new installment too, since Sterling K. Brown

00:04:08.129 --> 00:04:11.590
has also identified the movie as having a
"wicked sense of humor."

00:04:11.590 --> 00:04:13.930
It's not only Black who deserves credit for
that.

00:04:13.930 --> 00:04:18.360
The Predator's script was co-written by Black
and Fred Dekker, who previously collaborated

00:04:18.360 --> 00:04:20.900
on the horror-comedy cult classic The Monster
Squad.

00:04:23.180 --> 00:04:25.420
(the greatest movie line you'll hear all day)

00:04:26.020 --> 00:04:29.990
In other words, we're expecting this movie
to get weird, and considering how ridiculous

00:04:29.990 --> 00:04:34.610
this franchise has already gotten in the past,
that's saying something.

00:04:34.610 --> 00:04:36.490
The Busey legacy

00:04:36.490 --> 00:04:40.220
If you're concerned that this new movie may
neglect the past, one of the few characters

00:04:40.220 --> 00:04:43.460
we have confirmed details about should set
your mind at ease.

00:04:43.460 --> 00:04:48.120
Cast member Jake Busey has confirmed his role
in The Predator is the son of Peter Keyes,

00:04:48.120 --> 00:04:52.290
the character his father Gary Busey played
in 1990's Predator 2.

00:04:52.290 --> 00:04:57.169
An agent from the top-secret Other World Lifeforms
Taskforce, Keyes was a G-man who got his hands

00:04:57.169 --> 00:05:02.610
dirty, hunting and fighting the formidable
City Hunter with the help of some clever technology.

00:05:02.610 --> 00:05:06.440
He put in a pretty good effort, too, before
the predator got the fatal upper hand.

00:05:06.440 --> 00:05:10.190
We don't know a lot about Jake Busey's role
in The Predator yet, only that he's shared

00:05:10.190 --> 00:05:14.640
an on-set picture of himself in a lab coat,
and described his character as a doctor.

00:05:14.640 --> 00:05:18.569
Maybe Keyes' son ended up in the same branch
of government as his father, working more

00:05:18.569 --> 00:05:20.080
on the egghead side of things.

00:05:20.080 --> 00:05:24.009
Either way, you can bet one of two things
will happen in this pseudo-sequel, either

00:05:24.009 --> 00:05:28.440
the Predators will claim another Keyes family
member, or this son of a Busey is gonna pay

00:05:28.440 --> 00:05:32.130
off nearly 30 years of patience with some
glorious revenge.

00:05:32.130 --> 00:05:33.270
"Guess who's back?"

